          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "description": "Identify the artifact that is to be queried to complete the user request",
            "name": "Identify Artifact"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "select_artifact_metadata"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT",
          "id": "find_artifact",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "find_artifact_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUT\nUse the system input message as the complete user request:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nTASK\nChoose exactly one artifact from this allowed list:\n- projectCostTransactionDetails\n- unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails\n- projectAssetsView\n- projectAssetsViewExtract\n- projectAssetAssignmentsView\n- projectAssetLinesView\n- ProjectCostTransactionSummary\n- ProjectAssetLineSummary\n- unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract\n- projectContractInvoiceDetails\n- ProjectContractInvoiceSummary\n\nSELECTOR VALUE REQUIREMENT\nThe value of the \"artifact\" field must be exactly one artifact value from the allowed list above.\n\nCORE DECISION PRINCIPLE\nChoose the artifact by the user's business intent, not only by exact keywords. Infer whether the user wants individual business records or an aggregated answer. Do not require the user to say technical words such as transaction, record, detail, summary, analytic view, aggregate, or extract. Map natural business language to the artifact that best represents the underlying business object, granularity, and lifecycle context.\n\nOUTPUT DECISION ORDER\n1. First decide the business object family: processed project cost transactions, unprocessed project cost transactions, project assets, project asset assignments, project asset lines, or project contract invoices.\n2. Then decide granularity: detail rows or aggregated/summary measures.\n3. Then choose whether the aggregate can be handled by an existing analytic-summary selector or needs the business-view extract selector.\n4. When the question emphasizes asset lines and asks for totals, counts, comparison, grouping, status split, or cost/amount by project/business unit/task/asset/status, prefer `ProjectAssetLineSummary`.\n5. Do not route asset-line lifecycle/capitalization/transfer/assignment summary questions to cost transaction artifacts merely because the word cost appears.\n6. Do not route project contract invoice, billing invoice, invoice amount, invoice status, invoice date, bill-through date, credit memo, released/submitted/approved/rejected invoice, customer invoice, or contract billing invoice questions to project cost or project asset artifacts merely because the question mentions project, contract, cost, amount, or status.\n\nDETAIL VS SUMMARY RULE\n- Detail artifacts return individual rows/records.\n- Summary or extract artifacts return aggregated measures, grouped values, counts, totals, comparisons, or calculated results.\n- For project contract invoices, use `projectContractInvoiceDetails` for individual invoice records and `ProjectContractInvoiceSummary` for invoice aggregates, grouped measures, counts, totals, comparisons, rankings, or trends.\n- Summary intent includes total, count, sum, average, minimum, maximum, aggregate, summary, summarize, overall, rollup, breakdown, trend, distribution, comparison, grouped by, by a dimension, top/bottom/ranking, how much, how many, or X vs Y comparisons.\n- Detail intent includes show/list/display/get/find/view/retrieve/provide/give me records, entries, rows, details, line details, transaction history, or individual items when no aggregate/summary intent is present.\n- Existence wording such as are there or any is also detail intent unless the user explicitly requests a count, total, grouping, or calculation.\n- Project, task, date range, status, and attributes such as billable, capitalizable, or transferred are filters, not summary signals. Do not infer totals, counts, or grouping from filters or plural nouns such as costs or transactions.\n- If both detail and summary signals appear, choose the artifact that can answer the requested measure and grouping. Example: show total cost by task is summary even though it starts with show.\n\nEXTRACT SELECTOR RULES\nUse `projectAssetsViewExtract` for aggregate, grouped, comparison, ranking, or calculated questions about project assets themselves when the request is not about asset lines or asset assignments. This includes asset counts, totals, averages, min/max values, distributions, rankings, and grouped results over asset-level fields such as asset name, asset number, asset type, asset book, category, location, in-service date, retirement date, capitalization date, capitalized cost, total asset cost, project, task, or business unit.\nUse `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract` for aggregate, grouped, comparison, ranking, or calculated questions about unprocessed, pending, rejected, failed, errored, imported-but-not-processed, or not-yet-processed project cost transactions.\nDo not use an Extract selector for a request that asks for individual detail rows or record lists. Use `projectAssetsView` for asset detail rows, `projectAssetAssignmentsView` for project asset assignment detail rows, and `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails` for unprocessed cost transaction detail rows.\nDo not use `projectAssetsViewExtract` for asset-line lifecycle aggregate questions. Asset-line lifecycle aggregates still use `ProjectAssetLineSummary`.\n\nPROJECT CONTRACT INVOICE RULES\nUse `projectContractInvoiceDetails` for project contract invoice detail requests when the user asks for individual invoice records, invoice attributes, invoice lines, invoice history, or invoice-level details. This includes project contract invoices, contract billing invoices, customer invoices created from project contracts, draft/final invoices, credit memos, invoice numbers, invoice names, invoice dates, bill-through dates, invoice status, approval/release/submission/rejection status, transferred status, accepted status, accounting status, AR invoice references, contract/customer/sponsor, business unit, project, task, billing event, invoice amount, tax amount, currency, and invoice details filtered by project, contract, customer, business unit, date, status, or amount.\nUse `ProjectContractInvoiceSummary` when the project contract invoice request has aggregate, summary, comparison, ranking, trend, or grouped-measure intent. This includes total invoice amount, invoice counts, billed amount, unbilled or pending invoice amount when clearly invoice-related, approved/released/submitted/rejected invoice counts or amounts, invoice totals by project, contract, customer, sponsor, business unit, status, currency, invoice date, bill-through date, period, or invoice type, top/bottom invoices, and comparisons such as approved vs rejected invoices or invoice amount by customer.\nDo not choose `projectContractInvoiceDetails` or `ProjectContractInvoiceSummary` for project cost transactions, unprocessed costs, project assets, or asset-line lifecycle questions unless the wording clearly asks about invoices or project contract billing invoices.\nImportant invoice thin-line rules:\n- `invoice details`, `list invoices`, `show invoices`, `invoice status for invoice X`, or `which invoices` with no aggregate intent => `projectContractInvoiceDetails`.\n- `total invoice amount`, `how many invoices`, `invoice count`, `invoice amount by project/customer/contract/status`, `invoice trend`, or `compare invoices` => `ProjectContractInvoiceSummary`.\n- `billing` alone is not enough to choose an invoice artifact if the question is about billing events, billable costs, cost transactions, or project assets. Choose invoice artifacts only when the requested object is an invoice or contract billing invoice.\n\nPROJECT ASSET LINE SUMMARY RULES\nUse `ProjectAssetLineSummary` when the request is aggregate/summary/comparison in nature and emphasizes assets, asset lines, project asset lines, asset-line statuses, or asset lifecycle cost states.\n\nStrong `ProjectAssetLineSummary` signals include:\n- asset line, asset lines, project asset line, project asset lines\n- total/count/how many/sum/compare/break down/grouped by/task-wise/asset-wise/status-wise across asset lines\n- capitalized cost, transferred capitalized cost, pending capitalized cost, rejected capitalized cost\n- pending vs transferred, transferred vs pending, pending/transferred, pending/transferred\n- cost across all asset lines, asset-line costs by asset, asset-line costs by status, asset-line cost comparison, cost grouped by asset, cost by task for a project or business unit when the lifecycle context is asset lines\n- task-level capitalized cost within a project when the wording implies asset-line capitalization lifecycle\n- asset line count by project, business unit, asset, status, or task\n\nImportant thin-line rule:\n- `pending cost` alone may indicate `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails` for detail or `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract` for aggregate.\n- But `pending capitalized cost`, `pending asset line cost`, `pending assigned/unassigned/transferred cost`, or pending/transferred cost comparisons across asset lines are asset-line lifecycle summary requests. Choose `ProjectAssetLineSummary`.\n- `rejected cost` alone may indicate unprocessed/error transactions.\n- But `rejected capitalized cost` or `rejected asset line count/cost` is an asset-line status summary. Choose `ProjectAssetLineSummary`.\n\nASSET-LINE UNASSIGNED EXCEPTION\nThese are high-priority routing exceptions and override the normal aggregate-versus-detail rules:\n- Route any question about unassigned asset-line costs, unassigned costs on asset lines, asset-line costs where the asset is missing or not assigned, or costs associated with a missing asset to `projectAssetLinesView`.\n- Apply this exception whether the user asks for total, count, sum, average, comparison, grouping, status, details, records, rows, or any other aggregate or non-aggregate form.\n- Do not select `ProjectAssetLineSummary` for these exception cases, even when the wording contains total, sum, aggregate, summary, or comparison. The asset-line business view is the source for these scenarios.\n- This exception takes precedence over the normal `ProjectAssetLineSummary`, `projectAssetLinesView`, extract-selector, and generic pending-cost rules.\n\n\nPROJECT ASSET ASSIGNMENT RULES\nUse `projectAssetAssignmentsView` for detail or list requests about project asset assignments. This includes requests for individual assignment rows, assignment details, assignment attributes, assignment-related asset lists, and assignment records connected to project, task, common assignment, common-cost assignment, or project asset context when no aggregate, grouping, ranking, comparison, or calculation is requested.\nWhen the user asks for asset records by ordinary asset attributes and assignment context is not needed, use `projectAssetsView` for details or `projectAssetsViewExtract` for asset-level aggregate questions.\nDo not route asset-assignment questions to asset-line artifacts unless the request is specifically about asset line records or asset-line lifecycle measures.\n\nPROJECT ASSET DETAIL RULES\nUse `projectAssetsView` for asset-level detail requests about project assets, asset records, asset names, asset numbers, units, capitalized cost fields on asset records, total asset cost fields on asset records, asset book, asset type, asset location, category, in-service date, retirement date, reversal date, capitalization date, or asset lists when the user wants asset records rather than summarized asset measures.\n- If the question asks for a date or attribute of a named asset, choose `projectAssetsView`.\n- If the question asks for a list of assets by location, book, category, capital hold, transferred status, reversal status, pending tieback status, tied back status or capitalization status, choose `projectAssetsView` unless it asks for aggregated cost/count/comparison.\n- If the question asks for count, total, average, minimum, maximum, grouped values, trends, rankings, or comparisons over asset records, choose `projectAssetsViewExtract`.\n\nPROJECT ASSET LINE DETAIL RULES\nUse `projectAssetLinesView` for asset line detail requests when no aggregate/summary intent is present, such as listing individual asset line records, line-level details, asset line descriptions, asset line amounts, line items, or rows.\n\nCOST ARTIFACT GUIDANCE\nUse projectCostTransactionDetails for processed project cost detail requests. This includes requests for costs, cost records, cost entries, labor costs, usage costs, nonlabor costs, billable costs, nonbillable costs, capitalizable costs, inprogress costs, expenditure item costs, expenditure item details, transaction history, audit trails, or cost transactions filtered by project, task, person, supplier, invoice, purchase order, business unit, source, date, amount, status, or other attributes.\n\nUse ProjectCostTransactionSummary only when a processed project cost request has explicit summary intent, such as total costs, counts, summaries, trends, comparisons, rankings, breakdowns, or cost grouped by project, task, person, business unit, source, date, period, category, ledger, legal entity, cost organization, work type, cost type, or nonlabor resource.\n\nImportant cost thin-line rule:\nCost type alone is not summary. Questions such as \"show usage cost for project X\", \"show labor cost for project X\", or \"show billable cost for project X\" are detail requests unless the user explicitly asks for total, count, comparison, grouping, trend, breakdown, ranking, or cost by a dimension.\n\nUNPROCESSED COST RULES\nUse `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails` for rejected, failed, errored, imported-but-not-processed, pending, or not-yet-processed cost transaction detail requests when the wording points to transaction processing/import errors or generic pending/unprocessed costs, and not to asset-line lifecycle/capitalization/transfer/assignment summaries.\nUse `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract` for rejected, failed, errored, imported-but-not-processed, pending, or not-yet-processed cost transaction aggregate requests, including totals, counts, averages, min/max, grouped results, rankings, trends, breakdowns, and comparisons.\n\nTIEBREAKERS\n- Asset line focused + aggregate/summary/comparison/count/cost-by-dimension => `ProjectAssetLineSummary`.\n- Asset assignment focused + details/lists/assignment rows/assignment attributes/assignment-related asset lists with no aggregate intent => `projectAssetAssignmentsView`.\n- Asset focused + aggregate/summary/comparison/count/cost-by-dimension and not asset-line lifecycle or assignment-qualified => `projectAssetsViewExtract`.\n- Asset line focused + detail rows/no aggregation => `projectAssetLinesView`.\n- Asset focused + asset attributes/asset records/no aggregation => `projectAssetsView`.\n- Project contract invoice focused + aggregate/summary/comparison/count/total/grouping/ranking/trend => `ProjectContractInvoiceSummary`.\n- Project contract invoice focused + detail rows, invoice attributes, invoice lines, or individual invoice records/no aggregation => `projectContractInvoiceDetails`.\n- Cost focused + generic processed cost aggregate/no asset-line lifecycle or invoice terms => `ProjectCostTransactionSummary`.\n- Cost focused + generic processed cost details/no aggregate and no invoice terms => `projectCostTransactionDetails`.\n- Generic pending/rejected/unprocessed/import/error cost transaction wording + aggregate/summary/comparison/count/grouping => `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract`.\n- Generic pending/rejected/unprocessed/import/error cost transaction wording + detail rows/no aggregate => `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails`.\n- If the request mentions invoices with project, contract, customer, billing, amount, or status, choose `projectContractInvoiceDetails` or `ProjectContractInvoiceSummary` based on detail vs aggregate intent before considering cost or asset artifacts.\n- If the request mentions both assets and costs, do not automatically choose `projectAssetsView`; choose `ProjectAssetLineSummary` for asset-line lifecycle measures,  and `projectAssetsViewExtract` for asset-record aggregate measures.\n- If still uncertain, choose the most specific artifact that can answer the requested business object and granularity, then lower `confidencePercentage`.\n\nCONFIDENCE REQUIREMENTS\nReturn `confidencePercentage` as an integer from 0 to 100.\n- 95-100: direct match to one artifact by object and granularity.\n- 80-94: strong match with minor wording ambiguity.\n- 60-79: plausible match but missing some context.\n- Below 60: genuinely ambiguous; still choose the best artifact, but explain what is ambiguous.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\nReturn only valid JSON in this exact shape:\n{\n  \"artifact\": \"one allowed artifact\",\n  \"confidencePercentage\": 0,\n  \"explanation\": \"detailed reasoning including which part of the prompt strongly instructed to select one artifact\"\n}\n\nDo not return markdown. Do not return any text outside the JSON object."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"artifact\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"projectCostTransactionDetails\",\n        \"projectCostTransactionDetailsExtract\",\n        \"unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails\",\n        \"projectAssetsView\",\n        \"projectAssetsViewExtract\",\n        \"projectAssetAssignmentsView\",\n        \"projectAssetLinesView\",\n        \"ProjectCostTransactionSummary\",\n        \"ProjectAssetLineSummary\",\n        \"unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract\",\n        \"projectContractInvoiceDetails\",\n        \"ProjectContractInvoiceSummary\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"confidencePercentage\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"explanation\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"artifact\",\n    \"confidencePercentage\",\n    \"explanation\"\n  ]\n}\n",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Identify the artifact metadata for use while processing the user request",
            "name": "Select Artifact Metadata",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const artifact = ($context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT?.$output?.artifact ?? '').trim();\n\nconst metadataByArtifact = {\n  projectCostTransactionDetails: {\n    selector: 'projectCostTransactionDetails',\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectCostTransactions',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectCostTransaction',\n    view: 'projectCostTransactionDetails',\n    suggestedAlias: 'costTransactions',\n    artifactMetadata: $context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqOraErpCoreProjectCostTransactionsProjectCostTransactionDetailsBVMetadata\n  },\n  projectAssetsView: {\n    selector: 'projectAssetsView',\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectAsset',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectAsset',\n    view: 'projectAssetsView',\n    suggestedAlias: 'assets',\n    artifactMetadata: $context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqOraErpCoreProjectAssetProjectAssetsViewBVMetadata\n  },\n  projectAssetsViewExtract: {\n    selector: 'projectAssetsViewExtract',\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectAsset',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectAsset',\n    view: 'projectAssetsView',\n    suggestedAlias: 'assets',\n    artifactMetadata: $context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqOraErpCoreProjectAssetProjectAssetsViewBVMetadata\n  },\n  projectAssetAssignmentsView: {\n    selector: 'projectAssetAssignmentsView',\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectAsset',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectAssetAssignment',\n    view: 'projectAssetAssignmentsView',\n    suggestedAlias: 'assetAssignments',\n    artifactMetadata: $context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqOraErpCoreProjectAssetProjectAssetAssignmentsViewBVMetadata\n  },\n  projectAssetLinesView: {\n    selector: 'projectAssetLinesView',\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectAsset',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectAssetLine',\n    view: 'projectAssetLinesView',\n    suggestedAlias: 'assetLines',\n    artifactMetadata: $context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqOraErpCoreProjectAssetProjectAssetLinesViewBVMetadata\n  },\n  unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails: {\n    selector: 'unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails',\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectCostTransactions',\n    businessObject: 'UnprocessedProjectCostTransaction',\n    view: 'unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails',\n    suggestedAlias: 'unprocessedCosts',\n    artifactMetadata: $context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqOraErpCoreProjectCostTransactionsUnprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsBVMetadata\n  },\n  ProjectCostTransactionSummary: {\n    selector: 'ProjectCostTransactionSummary',\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectCostTransactions',\n    analyticView: 'ProjectCostTransactionSummary',\n    suggestedAlias: 'projectCostTransactionSummary',\n    artifactMetadata: $context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqProjectCostTransactionSummaryAVMetadata\n  },\n  ProjectAssetLineSummary: {\n    selector: 'ProjectAssetLineSummary',\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectAsset',\n    analyticView: 'ProjectAssetLineSummary',\n    suggestedAlias: 'projectAssetLineSummary',\n    artifactMetadata: $context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqProjectAssetLineSummaryAVMetadata\n  },\n  unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract: {\n    selector: 'unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract',\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectCostTransactions',\n    businessObject: 'UnprocessedProjectCostTransaction',\n    view: 'unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails',\n    suggestedAlias: 'unprocessedCosts',\n    artifactMetadata: $context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqOraErpCoreProjectCostTransactionsUnprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsBVMetadata\n  }\n};\n\nconst selected = metadataByArtifact[artifact] ?? {\n  selector: artifact,\n  module: null,\n  businessObject: null,\n  view: null,\n  suggestedAlias: null,\n  artifactMetadata: null\n};\n\nconst { artifactMetadata, ...targetConfig } = selected;\n\nreturn {\n  targetConfig,\n  artifactMetadata\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "set_selected_artifact_metadata"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_CODE_SELECT_ARTIFACT_METADATA",
          "id": "select_artifact_metadata",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
