        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Get the user session values for the user preferred date format",
            "errorNodeId": "1781496759182",
            "name": "Get User Session",
            "toolCode": "ORA_USER_SESSION_TOOL"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "2"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_TOOL_GET_USER_SESSION",
          "id": "3",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "TOOL"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Normalize exact dates and Business Unit wording, and isolate eligible business-view ordering instructions",
            "name": "Normalize User Input"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "check_extract_selector"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_LLM_NORMALIZE_USER_INPUT",
          "id": "2",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "2_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUTS\nOriginal user message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nSelected artifact:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT.$output.artifact}}\n\nUser preferred date format:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_TOOL_GET_USER_SESSION.$output.items[0].DateFormat}}\n\nCurrent runtime date context, if available:\n- currentDate: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nTASK\nNormalize the original user message before it is sent to BOSS Natural Language Search. Apply only the transformations defined below. Preserve every other part of the user's question as exactly as possible.\n\nTRANSFORMATION ORDER\n1. Inspect the original message and capture any removable ordering instruction verbatim before making any other changes.\n2. Remove that ordering instruction only when the selected artifact is one of the eligible BOSS business-view record artifacts listed below.\n3. Normalize Business Unit wording.\n4. Normalize exact dates using the existing date rules.\n\nBUSINESS UNIT NORMALIZATION\n- Replace every standalone occurrence matching Business Unit or BusinessUnit, case-insensitively and with whitespace between Business and Unit, with exactly BU.\n- Conceptually, match the whole phrase/token `business\\s*unit` with word boundaries.\n- Do not change larger words or unrelated text.\n\nORDERING EXTRACTION AND REMOVAL\nEligible BOSS business-view record artifacts:\n- projectCostTransactionDetails\n- unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails\n- projectAssetsView\n- projectAssetAssignmentsView\n- projectAssetLinesView\n- projectContractInvoiceDetails\n\n- An ordering instruction is only the portion of the question that asks to sort, order, rank, arrange, or sequence the displayed records, including its requested field(s), direction(s), priority, or tie-breaker when present. Examples include `sort by transaction date descending`, `order the results by amount from highest to lowest`, and `then by project number ascending`.\n- If the selected artifact is eligible and the message contains an ordering instruction, remove only the exact ordering portion. Do not remove or rewrite filters, requested fields, record limits, business criteria, date criteria, entities, or any other request content.\n- Set orderingRequest to the exact verbatim ordering portion from the original user message, preserving its original capitalization, spacing, punctuation, field names, and direction wording. Do not normalize Business Unit or dates inside orderingRequest.\n- Preserve conjunctions and punctuation that belong to the remaining question. Remove only punctuation or a connector when it belongs exclusively to the removed ordering clause and would otherwise leave malformed residue.\n- If the selected artifact is not eligible, do not remove ordering text and set orderingRequest to an empty string.\n- If no ordering instruction exists, set orderingRequest to an empty string.\n- Do not treat aggregate intent such as top 10, bottom 5, highest total, lowest cost, ranking questions, or comparisons as a removable display-ordering instruction unless the text explicitly asks to sort/order/arrange the records displayed.\n\nEXACT DATE NORMALIZATION\nExact date values include numeric dates, dates with month names, and date ranges with concrete date endpoints, such as 03/04/2026, 3 Apr, Apr 3, between 1/5 and 31/5, from May 1 to May 31, or transaction date 12.\n\nDo not rewrite relative date expressions such as last 20 days, last 1 week, this week, this month, this year, today, yesterday, tomorrow, next week, previous month, current quarter, fiscal year to date, or similar relative phrases.\n\nDo not rewrite date expressions if the value is indicated as a period name by qualifiers such as period, accounting period, asset period etc.\n\nDATE CONVERSION RULES\n1. Convert only exact date values to YYYY-MM-DD.\n2. Determine the user's preferred date format only from this value: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_TOOL_GET_USER_SESSION.$output.items[0].DateFormat}}.\n3. Assume exact input dates are written in the user's preferred date format.\n4. If a date clearly is not in the preferred format, infer the date format from the text and convert it to YYYY-MM-DD.\n5. If the year is omitted, use the current year from the current runtime date context. If no runtime date is available, use the model's current year.\n6. If the month is omitted, use the current month from the current runtime date context. If no runtime date is available, use the model's current month.\n7. Preserve all non-date text, project names, brackets, quoted text, amounts, and field names exactly as much as possible.\n8. Do not change date-like values that are identifiers, periods, project numbers, invoice numbers, task numbers, or amounts.\n9. Do not add explanatory text to the rewritten question.\n\nEXAMPLES\nEligible artifact input: Show Business Unit labor costs for project ABC with transaction dates between 4/1 and 4/30, sorted by transaction date descending\nIf preferred date format is MM/DD/YYYY and current year is 2026:\n- rewrittenQuestion: Show BU labor costs for project ABC with transaction dates between 2026-04-01 and 2026-04-30\n- orderingRequest: sorted by transaction date descending\n\nNon-eligible artifact input: Summarize businessunit costs ordered by total cost descending\n- Keep the ordering text in rewrittenQuestion because the selected artifact is not eligible.\n- Still normalize businessunit to BU.\n- orderingRequest must be an empty string.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\nReturn only valid JSON in this exact shape:\n{\n  \"rewrittenQuestion\": \"normalized user message\",\n  \"orderingRequest\": \"exact removed ordering text or empty string\",\n  \"explanation\": \"brief reason\"\n}\n\nIf no transformation applies, set rewrittenQuestion to the original user message unchanged. Do not return markdown. Do not return any text outside the JSON object."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"rewrittenQuestion\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"orderingRequest\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"explanation\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"rewrittenQuestion\",\n    \"orderingRequest\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Identify if the user request is to be processed by querying the identified business view artifact using the extract endpoint",
            "name": "Check Extract Selector"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "prepare_extract_query_payload",
            "false": "generate_bo_payload_for_bv"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_CONDITION_CHECK_EXTRACT_SELECTOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "prepare_filter_display_context",
          "id": "check_extract_selector",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "check_extract_selector_condition",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{['projectAssetsViewExtract','unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract'].includes($context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT.$output.artifact)}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Prepare extract query payload to process user request",
            "name": "Prepare Extract Query Request Payload"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "perform_extract_query"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_LLM_PREPARE_EXTRACT_QUERY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD",
          "id": "prepare_extract_query_payload",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "prepare_extract_query_payload_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUTS\nOriginal user message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nNormalized user message:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_NORMALIZE_USER_INPUT.$output.rewrittenQuestion}}\n\nSelected selector:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT.$output.artifact}}\n\nSelected artifact target config:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_CODE_SELECT_ARTIFACT_METADATA.$output.result.targetConfig}}\n\nSelected business view metadata:\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqSelectedArtifactMetadata}}\n\nBOSS extraction payload generation rules:\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqBvExtractPayloadGenerationRules}}\n\nTASK\nTransform the normalized user message into a Project Common Data Extraction EXTRACT payload.\nUse the selected artifact target config for module, businessObject, view, and suggested alias.\nUse the selected business view metadata as the only metadata source for exposed fields, accessors, labels, data types, searchable flags, sortable flags, enum metadata, and synonyms.\n\nPAYLOAD RULES\n1. Follow the BOSS extraction payload generation rules exactly.\n2. Use only fields and accessor field paths exposed by the selected business view metadata.\n3. Declare one source under viewQueries using the selected module, businessObject, and view.\n4. Populate fieldAliases for every field used by SELECT, WHERE, GROUP BY, ORDER BY, namedSelects, joins, or computed outputs.\n5. BQL must reference aliases from fieldAliases or outputs from namedSelects, not raw field paths.\n6. Use parameters for user-supplied scalar filter values when useful. Reference parameters as :parameterName in BQL and include the same names in parameters.\n7. Include namedSelects only when they simplify aggregation, grouping, normalization, ranking, UNION, or staged calculations.\n8. The top-level select must be a valid BQL SELECT statement and must alias computed output columns with readable names.\n9. Select-list relevance and ordering: include output columns directly required by the user question first. Then include other Project Management domain columns that make the answer useful and interpretable when they are relevant and exposed by the selected business view metadata, such as project, task, business unit, asset, transaction source, status, date, currency code, or unit of measure. Do not add unrelated columns just because they are available. Keep the SELECT list in the same business presentation order that should be shown to the user.\n10. Aggregate output rule: if the user asks for a single aggregate value, return a SELECT that produces that value plus any required context columns such as currency code or unit of measure. If the user asks for grouped, compared, ranked, or broken-down results, return the grouping dimensions first in business presentation order, then measures in business presentation order.\n11. Ordering rule: every final select must include an ORDER BY clause. Use the user's explicit sorting or ranking intent first. If the user does not specify sorting, choose the most meaningful Project Management business ordering for the question using selected output columns or sortable fields relevant to those output columns. For top, highest, largest, latest, newest, most recent, ranking, or greatest questions, order descending by the relevant measure or date. For bottom, lowest, smallest, earliest, oldest, or least questions, order ascending by the relevant measure or date. Use only sortable metadata fields or derived selected columns that can be ordered.\n12. Pagination rule: every final select must end with ORDER BY <chosen columns> OFFSET 0 ROWS FETCH NEXT 20 ROWS ONLY. Hard-code the offset to 0 and the row limit to 20. Do not use FETCH FIRST 25 ROWS ONLY for extract payloads.\n13. Serial-number rule: do not add ROWNUM, No, No., serial number, row number, sequence number, or any display-only numbering expression to the extract query payload. The downstream extract response formatter adds the display No. column.\n14. Aggregate cost and amount safety: when using aggregate functions over cost, amount, monetary, price, value, or currency-valued fields, include the associated currency code field from the selected business view metadata in fieldAliases, SELECT output, and GROUP BY. Do not aggregate monetary values across currencies. If the associated currency code field is not exposed by the selected business view metadata, do not include that aggregated cost or amount measure.\n15. Aggregate quantity safety: when summing or otherwise aggregating quantity fields, include the associated unit of measure or UOM field from the selected business view metadata in fieldAliases, SELECT output, and GROUP BY. Do not aggregate quantities across units of measure. If the associated unit of measure field is not exposed by the selected business view metadata, do not include that aggregated quantity measure.\n16. Unprocessed cost transaction safety: for selector unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract, never use cost fields or cost aggregates because costs may not have been calculated for unprocessed transactions. Do not select, filter, group, sort, aggregate, compute, or substitute fields whose names, labels, or descriptions indicate cost. Amount fields may be used only when explicitly requested, exposed by the metadata, and paired with the associated currency code as described above.\n17. Do not invent fields, accessors, enum values, filters, business units, project numbers, asset statuses, dates, currency codes, units of measure, costs, quantities, amounts, or ORDER BY columns.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\nReturn only a valid JSON object with this shape:\n{\n  \"parameters\": {},\n  \"viewQueries\": {\n    \"aliasName\": {\n      \"module\": \"moduleName\",\n      \"businessObject\": \"BusinessObjectName\",\n      \"view\": \"businessViewName\",\n      \"fieldAliases\": {\n        \"exposed.fieldPath\": \"bqlSafeAlias\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"namedSelects\": [\n    { \"name\": \"optionalIntermediateName\", \"select\": \"SELECT ...\" }\n  ],\n  \"select\": \"SELECT ...\"\n}\n\nOmit namedSelects when no intermediate query is needed. Omit parameters when no runtime scalar values are needed. Do not return markdown, comments, or text outside the JSON object."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": true\n    },\n    \"viewQueries\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": true\n    },\n    \"namedSelects\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"select\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"viewQueries\",\n    \"select\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": true\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
