        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Parse extract query response and prepare data for final user response",
            "name": "Generate Extract Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "prepare_filter_display_context"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_LLM_GENERATE_EXTRACT_RESPONSE",
          "id": "generate_extract_result",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "generate_extract_result_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUTS\nUser message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nSelected selector:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT.$output.artifact}}\n\nSelected artifact metadata for user-facing labels:\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqSelectedArtifactMetadata}}\n\nBOSS extract query payload:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_PREPARE_EXTRACT_QUERY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD.$output}}\n\nBOSS extract response:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_BO_FUNCTION_PERFORM_EXTRACT_QUERY.$output}}\n\nTASK\nGenerate only a compact JSON object that the Redwood Formatter can convert into chat-widget JSON.\n\nOUTPUT SHAPES\nFor text:\n{\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"result\": \"short user-facing message\",\n  \"explanation\": \"concise debug summary covering decision, data source, selected fields, templates, pairing, and amount/currency handling\"\n}\n\nFor table:\n{\n  \"type\": \"table\",\n  \"columns\": [\n    { \"headerText\": \"Column 1\", \"template\": \"\" },\n    { \"headerText\": \"Column 2\", \"template\": \"monetaryTemplate\" }\n  ],\n  \"data\": [\n    [\"row1 col1\", \"{amount:1250,currency:USD}\"],\n    [\"row2 col1\", \"{amount:2500,currency:USD}\"]\n  ],\n  \"explanation\": \"concise debug summary covering decision, data source, column order, templates, pairing, and amount/currency handling\"\n}\n\nDECISION AND DATA RULES\n1. Use BOSS extract response as the source data. The BOSS extract query payload explains how selected aliases and computed output columns map to business meaning.\n2. Use text when the user asks for a single summarized value or one answer, such as total, sum, count, how many, average, minimum, maximum, overall, or summary.\n3. Use table when the extract response contains multiple rows, or when the user asks to break down, list, show, display, compare, group, rank, or show values by a dimension.\n4. For text output, form a short natural-language answer using only mapped values from the extract response. Do not explain how you computed it.\n5. For every table output, include `No.` as the first column object in `columns` with `template` set to an empty string, and populate each row with a 1-based serial number as the first value.\n6. For table output, build user-friendly columns from meaningful selected aliases or computed column aliases in the query payload after the leading `No.` column. Do not use raw technical aliases if the payload exposes a clearer business label.\n7. Include filter dimensions or filter columns implied by the user message when those values are available in the extract response or can be mapped from the query payload.\n8. Preserve null values as null.\n9. If extract response has no rows or no usable values, return exact text 'No rows were found. '.\n\nDISPLAY LABEL RULES\n1. Use Selected artifact metadata as the primary source for every user-facing field label in both table column headers and text responses.\n2. Match extract response fields and query-payload aliases or computed output columns to metadata field paths, accessor paths, and labels. When a matching metadata entry exists, use its `label` exactly.\n3. For text responses, use metadata labels whenever naming the summarized measure, dimension, date, status, amount, count, or other business field.\n4. For table responses, use metadata labels for column `headerText`, including accessor-level labels for paired Number/Name values.\n5. If no matching metadata label exists, use a clear business label from the extract query payload. Humanize a technical alias only as the final fallback. Never expose a raw technical alias or field path when metadata or the query payload provides a business label.\n\nCOLUMN TEMPLATE RULES\n1. For every table output, return `columns` as an array of objects. Each object must contain `headerText` and `template`.\n2. Return the `columns` array as the only table column-definition structure. The `data` arrays must align positionally with the `columns` array.\n3. Allowed `template` values are exactly `monetaryTemplate`, `dateTemplate`, or an empty string `` for no template.\n4. Decide the template from the selected artifact metadata, query payload aliases, field labels, descriptions, data types, and source value semantics. Do not decide from the display header alone.\n5. Use `monetaryTemplate` for numeric measure columns so they are right aligned in the Redwood table. This includes true money, amount, cost, price, payment, rate, charge, total, value, revenue, expense, budget, balance, quantity, count, percentage, duration, and other columns whose displayed values are only numeric.\n6. For true money, amount, cost, price, payment, rate, charge, total, value, revenue, expense, budget, or balance columns with an associated currency code, the cell value should use Redwood amount schema such as `{amount:1250,currency:USD}`. Numeric non-money measure columns such as `Quantity` or `Count` may keep plain numeric values while still using `monetaryTemplate` for right alignment.\n7. Use `dateTemplate` only for true date or date-time columns. Date-template cell values should be dates or parseable date strings; the formatter will normalize them for Redwood rendering.\n8. Use empty template for `No.`, IDs, identifiers, codes, business numbers that identify records, names, statuses, sources, descriptions, units of measure, and business dimensions. Examples that must use empty template: `No.`, `Project Number`, `Task Number`, `Transaction Number`, `Invoice Number`, `Asset Number`, `Funding Source Number`, `Status`, `Document`, and `Asset Name`.\n9. Do not use `monetaryTemplate` for numeric-looking identifiers or code values, even when every value contains only digits. ID-like and number-like business keys are identifiers, not numeric measures.\n\nNUMBER/NAME PAIRING DISPLAY RULES\n1. When the source response contains both a Number/Code/Identifier value and a Name/Description/Display Name value for the same business attribute, combine them into one table column instead of returning separate columns.\n2. Apply this especially to Project, Task, Contract, Worker, Supplier, Customer, Asset, and similar business reference attributes when both values are available in the same row or mapped query output.\n3. The combined column header must be the accessor label from the selected artifact metadata, not a name/number composite label. Look up the label for the shared accessor or business reference attribute that owns both values. Examples: for `project.name` plus `project.projectNumber`, use the `project` accessor label `Project`; for `task.name` plus `task.taskNumber`, use the `task` accessor label `Project Task`; for `contract.contractName` plus `contract.contractNumber`, use `Contract`.\n4. If an accessor label is not available, use the clearest business reference label without Name, Number, Code, Identifier, Description, or Display Name suffixes.\n5. The combined cell value must be built from the two source values in the same format: `<name value> (<number value>)`. Example: `Store Expansion (PJT-1001)`.\n6. If one side is null, blank, or not present, do not invent it. Use the available value only, and use the accessor/business reference label for the header when available; otherwise use the matching single metadata label.\n7. Do not combine unrelated number/name fields from different accessors or business concepts. Only combine values that metadata, accessor path, query alias meaning, or source object nesting clearly identifies as the same attribute.\n8. The combined column uses empty template ``; do not use `monetaryTemplate` or `dateTemplate` for number/name pairing columns.\n\n\nREDWOOD AMOUNT/CURRENCY VALUE RULES\n1. The LLM is responsible for pairing money fields with currency fields from the same source row/object. Currency may be present in a non-displayed source field; it does not need to be selected as a table column.\n2. When a returned amount, cost, price, payment, rate, charge, total, value, revenue, expense, budget, or balance has an associated currency code anywhere in the same source row/object, return that value in Redwood amount schema string format in the same value position: `{amount:1250,currency:USD}` or `{amount:1250.50,currency:EUR}`.\n3. Numeric non-money measure columns such as quantity, count, percentage, duration, or other number-only measure values should not be converted into Redwood amount schema and should not invent a currency. They may remain plain numbers while their column uses `monetaryTemplate` for right alignment.\n4. Use one display column for the money value. Do not append currency as plain text such as `1250 USD`, do not put amount and currency into separate table columns when they can be paired, and do not mention currency separately for the same value.\n5. Treat fields named or labeled like currency, currencyCode, currencyCd, transactionCurrencyCode, projectCurrencyCode, ledgerCurrencyCode, enteredCurrencyCode, documentCurrencyCode, invoiceCurrencyCode, contractCurrencyCode, or similar as currency-code candidates.\n6. For text output, embed paired money values in the same Redwood amount schema string format, for example `The total burdened cost is {amount:1250,currency:USD}.`\n7. If you cannot safely identify the currency code for a money value, leave the money value as-is and do not invent a currency. Preserve null money values as null.\n\nEXPLANATION DEBUG RULES\n1. Always populate `explanation` with a concise debugging summary, not just the reason for choosing text or table.\n2. For table output, the explanation must briefly cover each major prompt section that affected the result: response format decision, source records used, selected fields and column order, column template choices, number/name pairing, and amount/currency handling.\n3. For text output, briefly cover response format decision, source values used, and why table-only rules such as column templates, pairing, and amount/currency formatting were not applicable or how they were applied.\n4. Keep `explanation` as a single JSON string. Do not include hidden chain-of-thought, step-by-step private reasoning, markdown, comments, or text outside the JSON object.\n\nGENERAL RULES\n1. Return only valid JSON.\n2. Do not return markdown, comments, or text outside the JSON object.\n3. Do not include hidden chain-of-thought in result. Use `explanation` only for the concise debug summary required above."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"type\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"columns\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"headerText\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"template\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"data\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"explanation\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"type\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Extract the query filters used while processing the user request",
            "name": "Prepare Filter Display Context",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const userMessage = ($context.$system.$inputMessage ?? '').trim();\nconst selectedArtifact = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT?.$output?.artifact ?? null;\nconst intelligentSearchOutputRaw = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_BO_FUNCTION_PERFORM_INTELLIGENT_SEARCH?.$output ?? {};\nconst extractQueryPayloadOutput = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_PREPARE_EXTRACT_QUERY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD?.$output ?? null;\n\nfunction normalizeString(value) {\n  return value == null ? '' : String(value).trim();\n}\n\nfunction parseJsonCandidate(value) {\n  if (value == null) return null;\n\n  if (typeof value === 'string') {\n    const normalized = value\n      .replace(/^```(?:json)?\\s*/i, '')\n      .replace(/\\s*```$/, '')\n      .trim();\n\n    if (!normalized || !/^[{\\[]/.test(normalized)) {\n      return null;\n    }\n\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(normalized);\n    } catch {\n      return null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return value;\n}\n\nconst intelligentSearchOutput = parseJsonCandidate(intelligentSearchOutputRaw)\n  ?? parseJsonCandidate(intelligentSearchOutputRaw?.result)\n  ?? intelligentSearchOutputRaw;\nconst avQueryPayload = intelligentSearchOutput?.queries?.[0] ?? null;\n\nfunction getFirstAnalyticViewFilter(queryPayload) {\n  const analyticViewCandidates = [\n    queryPayload?.analyticViews,\n    queryPayload?.query?.analyticViews,\n    queryPayload?.payload?.analyticViews\n  ];\n\n  for (const analyticViews of analyticViewCandidates) {\n    if (!analyticViews || typeof analyticViews !== 'object' || Array.isArray(analyticViews)) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    for (const analyticView of Object.values(analyticViews)) {\n      const filter = normalizeString(analyticView?.filter);\n      if (filter) {\n        return filter;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction formatExtractFilterValue(value) {\n  if (value == null) {\n    return 'null';\n  }\n  if (typeof value === 'number' || typeof value === 'boolean') {\n    return String(value);\n  }\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return `(${value.map(formatExtractFilterValue).join(', ')})`;\n  }\n  if (typeof value === 'object') {\n    return `'${JSON.stringify(value).replace(/'/g, \"''\")}'`;\n  }\n  return `'${String(value).replace(/'/g, \"''\")}'`;\n}\n\nfunction applyExtractFilterParameters(filter, parameters) {\n  if (!parameters || typeof parameters !== 'object' || Array.isArray(parameters)) {\n    return filter;\n  }\n\n  return filter.replace(/:([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*)\\b/g, (match, parameterName) => {\n    return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(parameters, parameterName)\n      ? formatExtractFilterValue(parameters[parameterName])\n      : match;\n  });\n}\n\nfunction applyExtractFieldAliases(filter, viewQueries) {\n  if (!viewQueries || typeof viewQueries !== 'object' || Array.isArray(viewQueries)) {\n    return filter;\n  }\n\n  const aliasToField = {};\n  const lowercaseAliasToField = {};\n  for (const [viewQueryNameValue, viewQuery] of Object.entries(viewQueries)) {\n    const viewQueryName = normalizeString(viewQueryNameValue);\n    const fieldAliases = viewQuery?.fieldAliases;\n    if (!fieldAliases || typeof fieldAliases !== 'object' || Array.isArray(fieldAliases)) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    for (const [fieldNameValue, aliasValue] of Object.entries(fieldAliases)) {\n      const fieldName = normalizeString(fieldNameValue);\n      const alias = normalizeString(aliasValue);\n      if (!fieldName || !alias) {\n        continue;\n      }\n\n      aliasToField[alias] = fieldName;\n      lowercaseAliasToField[alias.toLowerCase()] = fieldName;\n      if (viewQueryName) {\n        const qualifiedAlias = `${viewQueryName}.${alias}`;\n        aliasToField[qualifiedAlias] = fieldName;\n        lowercaseAliasToField[qualifiedAlias.toLowerCase()] = fieldName;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return filter.replace(/'(?:''|[^'])*'|[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(?:\\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)*/g, (token) => {\n    if (token.charAt(0) === \"'\") {\n      return token;\n    }\n    return aliasToField[token] ?? lowercaseAliasToField[token.toLowerCase()] ?? token;\n  });\n}\n\nfunction getExtractSelectFilter(payloadCandidate) {\n  const parsedOutput = parseJsonCandidate(payloadCandidate);\n  const parsedResult = parseJsonCandidate(parsedOutput?.result)\n    ?? parseJsonCandidate(payloadCandidate?.result);\n  const resultCandidate = parsedResult && typeof parsedResult === 'object'\n    ? parsedResult\n    : parsedOutput;\n  const parsedPayload = parseJsonCandidate(resultCandidate?.payload);\n  const parsed = parsedPayload && typeof parsedPayload === 'object'\n    ? parsedPayload\n    : resultCandidate;\n  const select = normalizeString(parsed?.select);\n  if (!select) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const whereMatch = /\\bwhere\\b/i.exec(select);\n  if (!whereMatch) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const afterWhere = select.slice(whereMatch.index + whereMatch[0].length).trim();\n  if (!afterWhere) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const nextClauseMatch = /\\b(group\\s+by|order\\s+by|offset|fetch|limit)\\b/i.exec(afterWhere);\n  const filter = normalizeString(nextClauseMatch ? afterWhere.slice(0, nextClauseMatch.index) : afterWhere);\n  if (!filter) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const filterWithValues = applyExtractFilterParameters(filter, parsed?.parameters);\n  return applyExtractFieldAliases(filterWithValues, parsed?.viewQueries);\n}\n\nconst bvFilter = intelligentSearchOutput?.queries?.[0]?.query?.collection?.filter ?? null;\nconst extractFilter = getExtractSelectFilter(extractQueryPayloadOutput);\nconst avFilter = getFirstAnalyticViewFilter(avQueryPayload);\n\nlet rawFilter = null;\nlet filterSource = 'NONE';\nif (normalizeString(bvFilter)) {\n  rawFilter = normalizeString(bvFilter);\n  filterSource = 'BV';\n} else if (normalizeString(extractFilter)) {\n  rawFilter = normalizeString(extractFilter);\n  filterSource = 'EXTRACT';\n} else if (normalizeString(avFilter)) {\n  rawFilter = normalizeString(avFilter);\n  filterSource = 'AV';\n}\n\nreturn {\n  rawFilter,\n  filterSource,\n  selectedArtifact,\n  shouldGenerateDisplayFilter: !!rawFilter,\n  userMessage\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "generate_filter_display_text"
          },
          "code": "PREPARE_FILTER_DISPLAY_CONTEXT",
          "id": "prepare_filter_display_context",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Generate the response section text to show the filters used while processing the user request",
            "name": "Generate Filter Display Text"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "prepare_text_result"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_FILTER_DISPLAY_TEXT",
          "id": "generate_filter_display_text",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "generate_filter_display_text_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUTS\nRaw filter:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_FILTER_DISPLAY_CONTEXT.$output.result.rawFilter}}\n\nFilter source:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_FILTER_DISPLAY_CONTEXT.$output.result.filterSource}}\n\nShould generate display filter:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_FILTER_DISPLAY_CONTEXT.$output.result.shouldGenerateDisplayFilter}}\n\nSelected artifact:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_FILTER_DISPLAY_CONTEXT.$output.result.selectedArtifact}}\n\nSelected artifact metadata:\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarUqSelectedArtifactMetadata}}\n\nTASK\nConvert the raw technical filter into a short user-facing filter summary for display above the result.\n\nOUTPUT CONTRACT\nReturn only valid JSON:\n{\n  \"displayText\": \"Filters applied: Field Label: value; Other Field: value\",\n  \"explanation\": \"Concise diagnostic summary of the source, retained and omitted predicates, label resolution, and applicable formatting rules.\"\n}\n\nWhen no displayable filter should be shown, return an empty `displayText` and explain which empty-output rule applied.\n\nWHEN TO RETURN EMPTY\nReturn an empty `displayText` when:\n- `shouldGenerateDisplayFilter` is false\n- `rawFilter` is empty\n- no clear user-facing field or value can be identified\n- only technical grain, hierarchy, implementation, alias, metadata, or row-limit predicates remain\n\nSOURCE AND METADATA RULES\n1. For BV and Extract filters, use selected artifact metadata to resolve business labels where available.\n2. For AV filters, use the raw filter clause as the only evidence for filtered fields and values. Use selected artifact metadata only as the AV display-label map.\n3. For AV filters, first look up the exact raw AV field path in selected artifact metadata, including technical member suffixes such as `.$memberName` and `.$memberDescription`.\n4. When an exact mapping exists, use its mapped label exactly. Do not append Name, Description, Code, or another suffix.\n5. If no exact mapping exists, remove technical suffixes such as `.$memberDescription`, `.$memberName`, and `.$levelName`, then try the simplified field path in selected artifact metadata.\n6. If neither exact nor simplified metadata lookup succeeds, use the path-based label derivation rules below. Never expose technical tokens such as `$memberName`, `$memberDescription`, or `$levelName` in `displayText`.\n7. Omit AV hierarchy, grain, and implementation predicates, especially fields ending in `.$levelName`, regardless of their values.\n\nPROJECT COST TRANSACTION SUMMARY LEDGER RULE\nWhen `selectedArtifact` is exactly `ProjectCostTransactionSummary`, treat the predicate `providerLedger.ledgerSetName = 'All Ledgers'` as a technical default constraint. Omit it from `displayText`; do not convert it into a business label or value, and do not count it as a retained business predicate. Apply this rule only to the value `All Ledgers`; handle other provider-ledger predicates normally.\n\nAV PERIOD LEVEL LABEL RULES\n1. When an AV filter contains a period-dimension predicate ending in `.$levelName`, use its value only as label context for a business predicate on the same dimension. Do not display the `.$levelName` predicate itself.\n2. Derive the base label for the related business predicate from selected artifact metadata using the normal exact-path and simplified-path lookup rules.\n3. If the related `.$levelName` value is `QUARTER`, append ` Quarter Number` to the base label. If it is `YEAR`, append ` Year` to the base label. If it is `PERIOD`, retain the base label unchanged.\n4. Example: `providerProjectAccountingPeriod.$memberName = 'Q1' AND providerProjectAccountingPeriod.$levelName = 'QUARTER'` becomes `Filters applied: Project Accounting Period Quarter Number: Q1` when the metadata-derived base label is `Project Accounting Period`.\n\nDISPLAY RULES\n1. Output must be business-readable and compact.\n2. Do not display labels such as Lookup Code, Lookup Type, Lookup Code Meaning, ID, Identifier, or Code when the field represents a business concept through an accessor.\n3. Preserve user-provided values exactly after removing SQL quotes and `TO_DATE` wrappers, except for the explicit code-to-meaning mappings in this prompt.\n4. For multiple entries, separate entries with semicolons. Prefer at most four entries; omit technical or lower-value predicates first.\n5. If `displayText` is non-empty, it must start exactly with `Filters applied:` and remain one line.\n\nFIELD LABEL RULES\nChoose one concise business label for each filtered field, in this order:\n1. For AV filters, first use an exact raw field-path mapping from selected artifact metadata. If unavailable, use the simplified AV field-path mapping after removing technical member suffixes.\n2. For an accessor with a generic leaf field such as `name`, `meaning`, `displayName`, `lookupCode`, `lookupType`, `id`, `code`, `number`, `identifier`, `memberName`, or `memberDescription`, use the accessor’s label.\n3. For OR conditions over alternate identifiers of the same business concept, collapse them to one label and one non-empty value:\n   - `project.name = 'X' OR project.projectNumber = 'X'` → `Project: X`\n   - If no value is displayable, show only the concept label.\n4. For a specific meaningful leaf field, use full-path metadata when available.\n5. Otherwise derive a business-readable label using these fallbacks:\n   - `project.projectNumber`, `project.name`, `project.$memberName`, `project.$memberDescription` → Project\n   - `task.taskNumber`, `task.name`, `projectTask.$memberName`, `projectTask.$memberDescription` → Task\n   - `task.topTask.name`, `projectTask.topTaskName` → Top Task\n   - `businessUnit.name`, `businessUnit.$memberDescription` → Business Unit\n   - `transactionSource.name` → Transaction Source\n   - `person.names.displayName` → Person\n   - `supplier.name` → Supplier\n   - `billable.meaning`, `billable.$memberDescription` → Billable\n   - `capitalizable.meaning`, `capitalizable.$memberDescription` → Capitalizable\n   - `assetType.meaning` → Asset Type\n   - `assetBook.name` → Asset Book\n   - `projectAsset.assetNumber`, `projectAsset.assetName` → Asset\n6. Use common business nouns instead of technical path names.\n\nCONDITION SIMPLIFICATION\n1. Separate retained AND predicates into semicolon-delimited entries.\n2. Omit technical predicates, including hierarchy grain, row limits, and alias-only constraints.\n3. Summarize these boolean/null patterns by business intent:\n   - `netZeroItemFlag = false OR netZeroItemFlag = null` → `Net Zero Item: No`\n   - `netZeroItemFlag != true`, `NOT netZeroItemFlag`, or `netZeroItemFlag = false` → `Net Zero Item: No`\n   - `unmatchedTransactionFlag = true` → `Unmatched Transaction: Yes`\n4. Display lookup-meaning filters using the business label and value, for example `Billable: Yes`, `Capitalizable: No`, or `Status: Rejected`.\n5. When a business condition includes implementation cleanup such as `OR field = null`, display only the business value.\n6. If a condition is too technical to summarize accurately but clearly belongs to one concept, display only that concept label.\n\nCODE-TO-MEANING MAPPINGS\nApply mappings only to the specified field and artifact context. For list/`IN` filters, map each recognized value in original order. Preserve unrecognized values exactly.\n\nCost Classification\nApply only when `selectedArtifact` is `projectCostTransactionDetails` or `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails` and the filter is for Cost Classification:\n- BTC -> Burden Transaction\n- ER -> Expense Reports\n- INV -> Inventory\n- OT -> Overtime\n- PJ -> Miscellaneous Transaction\n- ST -> Straight Time\n- USG -> Usages\n- VI -> Supplier Invoices\n- WIP -> Work-In-Process\n\nTransaction Status\nApply only to `transactionStatus.lookupCode`:\n- R -> Rejected\n- P -> Pending\n\nAdjustment Status\nApply only to `adjustmentStatus.lookupCode`:\n- P -> Pending\n- R -> Rejected\n\nAsset Type\nApply only to `assetType.lookupCode`:\n- AS-BUILT -> As-built\n- RETIREMENT_ADJUSTMENT -> Retirement adjustment\n\nAsset Line Status\nApply only when `selectedArtifact` is `projectAssetLinesView` and the field is `status.lookupCode`:\n- P -> Pending\n- T -> Transferred\n- R -> Rejected\n\nAsset Line Status (AV)\nApply only when `selectedArtifact` is `ProjectAssetLineSummary` and the raw filter field is `projectAssetLineStatus.$memberName`:\n- P -> Pending\n- T -> Transferred\n- R -> Rejected\n\nAsset, Project, Task\nApply only when `selectedArtifact` is `ProjectAssetAssignmentsView`, `ProjectAssetLinesView` or `ProjectAssetsView` and the raw filter field is `projectAsset.id`,`asset.assetId`, `project.id`,`task.id`:\n- 0 -> None\n- null -> None\n\nBOOLEAN FLAG VALUE MAPPING\nApply only when `selectedArtifact` is `projectCostTransactionDetails`, `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails`, or `unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetailsExtract` and the filtered field is Billable or Capitalizable (including its exposed accessor or lookup field):\n- Y → Yes\n- N → No\n\nOPERATOR DISPLAY RULES\n1. Never display raw operators such as `=`, `<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=`, `!=`, `<>`, `IN`, `LIKE`, or `BETWEEN`.\n2. Equality: `Field Label: value`.\n3. List filters: `Field Label: value1, value2`.\n4. Numeric comparisons:\n   - `> value` → greater than value\n   - `>= value` → greater than or equal to value\n   - `< value` → less than value\n   - `<= value` → less than or equal to value\n5. Date/date-time comparisons:\n   - `> date` → after date\n   - `>= date` → on or after date\n   - `< date` → before date\n   - `<= date` → on or before date\n6. Combine same-field ranges:\n   - date range → `Field Label: start - end`\n   - amount range → `Field Label: low - high`\n7. Use simple wording for not-equal conditions, for example `Status: not Rejected`; otherwise show only the label.\n8. For `LIKE` or contains filters, use `Field Label: contains value` and remove matching-only wildcards.\n9. Display `TO_DATE('01/05/2026','DD/MM/YYYY')` as `01/05/2026`.\n\nEXPLANATION RULES\n1. Keep `explanation` to at most three short sentences.\n2. State the source used, retained and omitted predicates, label-resolution method, and any relevant mapping or formatting rule.\n3. For empty output, state the specific empty-output rule.\n4. Do not include markdown, hidden reasoning, confidence estimates, or unsupported assumptions.\n\nFINAL RULES\n- Return exactly the two JSON fields: `displayText` and `explanation`.\n- Do not return markdown, comments, or text outside the JSON object."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"displayText\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"explanation\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"displayText\",\n    \"explanation\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Prepare the final response of the user query",
            "name": "Format Response",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const workflowCode = ($context.$workflow?.$name ?? 'ORA_PRJ_PJC_PROJECT_FINANCIAL_INQUIRY_ASSISTANT_TEAM').trim();\nconst workflowDescription = 'Provides instant and clear explanations for any project financial transaction status using natural language dialogue and direct access to detailed audit trails and supporting data.';\nconst userMessage = ($context.$system.$inputMessage ?? '').trim();\nconst intelligentSearchOutput = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_BO_FUNCTION_PERFORM_INTELLIGENT_SEARCH?.$output ?? {};\nconst bvFormatterOutput = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_GENERATE_BUSINESS_VIEW_RESPONSE?.$output ?? {};\nconst avFormatterOutput = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_GENERATE_ANALYTICS_RESPONSE?.$output ?? {};\nconst extractFormatterOutput = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_GENERATE_EXTRACT_RESPONSE?.$output ?? {};\nconst filterDisplayContext = $context.$nodes.PREPARE_FILTER_DISPLAY_CONTEXT?.$output?.result ?? {};\nconst filterDisplayOutput = $context.$nodes.GENERATE_FILTER_DISPLAY_TEXT?.$output ?? {};\nconst returnedFilters = filterDisplayContext.rawFilter ?? userMessage ?? null;\nconst bossArtifact = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT?.$output?.artifact ?? null;\nconst analyticsExtractOutput = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_BO_FUNCTION_RUN_ANALYTICS_EXTRACT_QUERY?.$output ?? {};\nconst commonExtractOutput = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_BO_FUNCTION_PERFORM_EXTRACT_QUERY?.$output ?? {};\nconst TABLE_DISPLAY_LIMIT = 20;\nconst TABLE_LIMIT_NOTICE = 'Showing the first 20 rows only. ';\n\nfunction normalizeString(value) {\n  return value == null ? '' : String(value).trim();\n}\n\nfunction parseJsonCandidate(value) {\n  if (value == null) return null;\n\n  if (typeof value === 'string') {\n    const normalized = value\n      .replace(/^```(?:json)?\\s*/i, '')\n      .replace(/\\s*```$/, '')\n      .trim();\n\n    if (!normalized) return null;\n\n    if (!/^[{\\[]/.test(normalized)) {\n      return null;\n    }\n\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(normalized);\n    } catch {\n      return null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return value;\n}\n\nfunction getReturnedFiltersFromRelevantInfo(value) {\n  const parsed = parseJsonCandidate(value);\n  if (!parsed || typeof parsed !== 'object' || Array.isArray(parsed)) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  return parsed.atomicAgentDetails?.filters ?? null;\n}\n\nfunction isFormatterPayload(value) {\n  return value && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value) && normalizeString(value.type);\n}\n\nfunction isMultiFormatterPayload(value) {\n  return Array.isArray(value) && value.some(isFormatterPayload);\n}\n\nfunction resolveFormatterPayload() {\n  const candidates = [\n    extractFormatterOutput,\n    extractFormatterOutput?.result,\n    avFormatterOutput,\n    avFormatterOutput?.result,\n    bvFormatterOutput,\n    bvFormatterOutput?.result\n  ];\n\n  for (const candidate of candidates) {\n    const parsed = parseJsonCandidate(candidate);\n    if (isFormatterPayload(parsed) || isMultiFormatterPayload(parsed)) {\n      return parsed;\n    }\n    if (parsed && typeof parsed === 'object' && !Array.isArray(parsed) && isMultiFormatterPayload(parsed.items)) {\n      return parsed.items;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return {\n    type: 'text',\n    result: 'Sorry, I could not prepare the result right now. Please try again or refine your request.',\n    explanation: 'Fallback response because the post-BOSS formatter output was unavailable.'\n  };\n}\n\nfunction toFieldName(columnName, index, usedNames) {\n  const base = String(columnName ?? '')\n    .replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]+/g, ' ')\n    .trim()\n    .split(/\\s+/)\n    .filter(Boolean)\n    .map((part, partIndex) => {\n      const lower = part.toLowerCase();\n      return partIndex === 0 ? lower : lower.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + lower.slice(1);\n    })\n    .join('');\n\n  let fieldName = base || `column${index + 1}`;\n  if (/^[0-9]/.test(fieldName)) {\n    fieldName = `column${fieldName}`;\n  }\n\n  let uniqueName = fieldName;\n  let suffix = 2;\n  while (usedNames.has(uniqueName)) {\n    uniqueName = `${fieldName}${suffix}`;\n    suffix += 1;\n  }\n  usedNames.add(uniqueName);\n  return uniqueName;\n}\n\nfunction looksLikeFormatterMarkup(value) {\n  return /^\\{(?:amount|date):.+\\}$/.test(normalizeString(value));\n}\n\nfunction isDateLikeValue(value) {\n  if (value == null) {\n    return false;\n  }\n  if (value instanceof Date) {\n    return !Number.isNaN(value.getTime());\n  }\n  const normalized = normalizeString(value);\n  if (!normalized || looksLikeFormatterMarkup(normalized) || /^-?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?$/.test(normalized)) {\n    return false;\n  }\n  const looksDateLike = [\n    /^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}(?:[T\\s].*)?$/,\n    /^\\d{1,2}[/-]\\d{1,2}[/-]\\d{2,4}(?:\\s+\\d{1,2}:\\d{2}(?::\\d{2})?)?$/,\n    /^(?:Jan|Feb|Mar|Apr|May|Jun|Jul|Aug|Sep|Sept|Oct|Nov|Dec)[a-z]*\\s+\\d{1,2},?\\s+\\d{2,4}$/i,\n    /^\\d{1,2}\\s+(?:Jan|Feb|Mar|Apr|May|Jun|Jul|Aug|Sep|Sept|Oct|Nov|Dec)[a-z]*\\s+\\d{2,4}$/i\n  ].some((pattern) => pattern.test(normalized));\n  return looksDateLike && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(normalized));\n}\n\nfunction formatDateForMarkup(value) {\n  const date = value instanceof Date ? value : new Date(normalizeString(value));\n  if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  const pad = (part) => String(part).padStart(2, '0');\n  return `${date.getFullYear()}-${pad(date.getMonth() + 1)}-${pad(date.getDate())}`;\n}\n\nfunction buildDateMarkup(value) {\n  const normalized = normalizeString(value);\n  if (!normalized || !isDateLikeValue(normalized)) {\n    return value;\n  }\n  const formattedDate = formatDateForMarkup(normalized);\n  return formattedDate ? `{date:${formattedDate}}` : value;\n}\n\nfunction decorateTextSegment(segment) {\n  return segment.replace(/\\b\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}(?:[T\\s][0-9:.+\\-Z]*)?\\b/g, (match) => {\n    return isDateLikeValue(match) ? buildDateMarkup(match) : match;\n  });\n}\n\nfunction decorateTextValue(text) {\n  const normalized = normalizeString(text);\n  if (!normalized) {\n    return normalized;\n  }\n  const markupPattern = /(\\{(?:amount|date):[^}]+\\})/g;\n  return normalized\n    .split(markupPattern)\n    .map((segment) => (/^\\{(?:amount|date):[^}]+\\}$/.test(segment) ? segment : decorateTextSegment(segment)))\n    .join('');\n}\n\nfunction formatTimestamp(date) {\n  const pad = (value) => String(value).padStart(2, '0');\n  return `${pad(date.getDate())}-${pad(date.getMonth() + 1)}-${date.getFullYear()} ${pad(date.getHours())}:${pad(date.getMinutes())}`;\n}\n\nfunction buildTextResponse(payload) {\n  const text = normalizeString(payload.result);\n  if (!text) {\n    throw new Error('Text formatter payload must contain a non-empty result string.');\n  }\n  return {\n    display_type: 'text',\n    display_sequence: 1,\n    text: decorateTextValue(text),\n    expand: {\n      display: 'true',\n      headerText: 'Summary'\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nfunction normalizeTemplateValue(value) {\n  return value === 'monetaryTemplate' || value === 'dateTemplate' ? value : '';\n}\n\nfunction normalizeColumnDefinition(column, index, usedNames) {\n  const source = column && typeof column === 'object' && !Array.isArray(column)\n    ? column\n    : { headerText: column };\n  const headerText = normalizeString(source.headerText || source.label || source.name || source.field || `Column ${index + 1}`) || `Column ${index + 1}`;\n  return {\n    headerText,\n    field: toFieldName(headerText, index, usedNames),\n    template: normalizeTemplateValue(source.template)\n  };\n}\n\nfunction formatDisplayValue(value, column) {\n  if (column.template === \"monetaryTemplate\") {\n    return value == null ? null : String(value);\n  }\n  if (value == null || looksLikeFormatterMarkup(value)) {\n    return value;\n  }\n  if (column.template === 'dateTemplate' && isDateLikeValue(value)) {\n    return buildDateMarkup(value);\n  }\n  return value;\n}\n\nfunction buildTableResponse(payload) {\n  const originalColumns = Array.isArray(payload.columns) ? payload.columns : null;\n  const originalData = Array.isArray(payload.data) ? payload.data : null;\n  if (!originalColumns || !originalData) {\n    throw new Error('Table formatter payload must contain columns and data arrays.');\n  }\n\n  const usedFieldNames = new Set();\n  const definitions = originalColumns.map((column, index) => normalizeColumnDefinition(column, index, usedFieldNames));\n\n  const rows = originalData.map((rowValues) => {\n    const normalizedRow = Array.isArray(rowValues) ? rowValues : [];\n    return definitions.reduce((row, column, columnIndex) => {\n      row[column.field] = formatDisplayValue(normalizedRow[columnIndex] ?? null, column);\n      return row;\n    }, {});\n  });\n\n  const columns = definitions.map((column) => ({\n    headerText: column.headerText,\n    field: column.field,\n    className: '',\n    resizable: 'enabled',\n    id: column.field,\n    template: column.template\n  }));\n\n  const primaryKeyField = definitions[0]?.field ?? 'column1';\n\n  return {\n    display_type: 'table',\n    display_sequence: 1,\n    rows: {\n      items: rows\n    },\n    columns: {\n      items: columns\n    },\n    keyAttributes: {\n      items: [primaryKeyField]\n    },\n    accessibility: {\n      'aria-label': userMessage ? `Results table for ${userMessage}` : 'Project financial inquiry results',\n      'row.accessible-row-header': primaryKeyField\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nfunction cloneFormatterPayload(payload) {\n  if (Array.isArray(payload)) {\n    return payload.map(cloneFormatterPayload);\n  }\n  if (payload && typeof payload === 'object') {\n    return { ...payload };\n  }\n  return payload;\n}\n\nfunction isTableFormatterPayload(payload) {\n  return payload && typeof payload === 'object' && !Array.isArray(payload)\n    && normalizeString(payload.type).toLowerCase() === 'table'\n    && Array.isArray(payload.columns)\n    && Array.isArray(payload.data);\n}\n\nfunction firstArrayAtPaths(source, paths) {\n  for (const path of paths) {\n    let value = source;\n    for (const part of path) {\n      value = value?.[part];\n    }\n    if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n      return value;\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction findFirstDataArray(value, depth = 0) {\n  if (depth > 4 || value == null) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return value;\n  }\n  if (typeof value !== 'object') {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const preferredKeys = ['items', 'rows', 'data', 'result', 'results', 'values'];\n  for (const key of preferredKeys) {\n    const nested = findFirstDataArray(value[key], depth + 1);\n    if (nested) {\n      return nested;\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const nestedValue of Object.values(value)) {\n    const nested = findFirstDataArray(nestedValue, depth + 1);\n    if (nested) {\n      return nested;\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction getUpstreamReturnedRows() {\n  const bvRows = firstArrayAtPaths(intelligentSearchOutput, [\n    ['queries', 0, 'data', 'items'],\n    ['queries', 0, 'data', 'rows'],\n    ['queries', 0, 'data']\n  ]);\n  if (bvRows) {\n    return bvRows;\n  }\n\n  const avRows = findFirstDataArray(analyticsExtractOutput);\n  if (avRows) {\n    return avRows;\n  }\n\n  return findFirstDataArray(commonExtractOutput);\n}\n\nfunction applyTableDisplayLimit(payload) {\n  const returnedRows = getUpstreamReturnedRows();\n  if (!Array.isArray(returnedRows) || returnedRows.length <= TABLE_DISPLAY_LIMIT) {\n    return payload;\n  }\n\n  const payloadItems = Array.isArray(payload) ? payload : [payload];\n  const normalizedItems = payloadItems\n    .filter(isFormatterPayload)\n    .map(cloneFormatterPayload);\n  const firstTableIndex = normalizedItems.findIndex(isTableFormatterPayload);\n  if (firstTableIndex === -1) {\n    return payload;\n  }\n\n  normalizedItems[firstTableIndex] = {\n    ...normalizedItems[firstTableIndex],\n    data: Array.isArray(normalizedItems[firstTableIndex].data)\n      ? normalizedItems[firstTableIndex].data.slice(0, TABLE_DISPLAY_LIMIT)\n      : normalizedItems[firstTableIndex].data\n  };\n\n  const nonNoticeItems = normalizedItems.filter((item) => {\n    return !(normalizeString(item.type).toLowerCase() === 'text' && normalizeString(item.result) === TABLE_LIMIT_NOTICE);\n  });\n\n  return [\n    {\n      type: 'text',\n      result: TABLE_LIMIT_NOTICE,\n      explanation: 'Deterministic notice because the upstream data source returned more than 20 records.'\n    },\n    ...nonNoticeItems\n  ];\n}\n\nfunction getFilterDisplayText() {\n  return normalizeString(filterDisplayOutput.displayText ?? filterDisplayOutput?.result?.displayText);\n}\n\nfunction appendFilterDisplayText(payload) {\n  const filterText = getFilterDisplayText();\n  if (!filterText) {\n    return payload;\n  }\n\n  const payloadItems = (Array.isArray(payload) ? payload : [payload])\n    .filter(isFormatterPayload)\n    .map(cloneFormatterPayload);\n  const hasTableOutput = payloadItems.some(isTableFormatterPayload);\n  const lastTextIndex = payloadItems.map((item, index) => ({ item, index })).reverse()\n    .find(({ item }) => normalizeString(item.type).toLowerCase() === 'text')?.index;\n\n  if (lastTextIndex != null) {\n    const existingText = normalizeString(payloadItems[lastTextIndex].result);\n    const separator = hasTableOutput ? ' ' : '<br>';\n    payloadItems[lastTextIndex] = {\n      ...payloadItems[lastTextIndex],\n      result: existingText ? `${existingText}${separator}${filterText}` : filterText\n    };\n    return payloadItems;\n  }\n\n  return [\n    {\n      type: 'text',\n      result: filterText,\n      explanation: 'Filter display text generated from applied filters.'\n    },\n    ...payloadItems\n  ];\n}\n\nfunction buildResponseItem(payload, sequence) {\n  const payloadType = normalizeString(payload.type).toLowerCase();\n  let item;\n  if (payloadType === 'text') {\n    item = buildTextResponse(payload);\n  } else if (payloadType === 'table') {\n    item = buildTableResponse(payload);\n  } else {\n    throw new Error('Formatter output item must contain type \"text\" or \"table\".');\n  }\n  item.display_sequence = sequence;\n  return item;\n}\n\nconst formatterPayload = appendFilterDisplayText(applyTableDisplayLimit(resolveFormatterPayload()));\nconst responseItems = (Array.isArray(formatterPayload) ? formatterPayload : [formatterPayload])\n  .filter(isFormatterPayload)\n  .map((payload, index) => buildResponseItem(payload, index + 1));\nif (responseItems.length === 0) {\n  throw new Error('Formatter output must contain at least one type \"text\" or \"table\" item.');\n}\n\nreturn {\n  agent: workflowCode.toLowerCase(),\n  intent: 'ProjectFinancialInquiry',\n  schema_version: '1',\n  title: 'Project Financial Inquiry',\n  description: workflowDescription,\n  timestamp: formatTimestamp(new Date()),\n  topicName: 'Project Financial Inquiry',\n  atomicAgentDetails: {\n    atomicAgentCode: workflowCode,\n    atomicAgentContext: bossArtifact,\n    contextDetails: {\n      searchQuery: userMessage\n    },\n    filters: returnedFilters,\n    atomicAgentResponse: {}\n  },\n  agent_response: responseItems\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "return_implementation_in_progress"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_CODE_FORMAT_RESPONSE",
          "id": "prepare_text_result",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Return the final json response.",
            "name": "Return Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_RETURN_RETURN_RESPONSE",
          "id": "return_implementation_in_progress",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "return_implementation_in_progress_value",
              "name": "returnValue",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_CODE_FORMAT_RESPONSE.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "RETURN"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Prepare the payload for calling the Intelligent Search end point",
            "name": "Prepare Intelligent Search Request Payload",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const originalUserMessage = ($context.$system.$inputMessage ?? '').trim();\nconst dateRewriteOutput = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_NORMALIZE_USER_INPUT?.$output ?? {};\nconst rewrittenQuestion = typeof dateRewriteOutput.rewrittenQuestion === 'string'\n  ? dateRewriteOutput.rewrittenQuestion.trim()\n  : '';\nconst userMessage = rewrittenQuestion || originalUserMessage;\nconst artifact = ($context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT?.$output?.artifact ?? '').trim();\n\nlet queryConfig = null;\nlet target;\nif (artifact === 'projectCostTransactionDetails') {\n  target = {\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectCostTransactions',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectCostTransaction',\n    businessView: 'projectCostTransactionDetails'\n  };\n\n  queryConfig = {\n    fields: [\n      'transactionNumber',\n      'transactionDate',\n      'quantity',\n      'burdenedCostInTransactionCurrency'\n    ],\n    accessors: {\n      project: {\n        fields: ['projectNumber', 'name']\n      },\n      task: {\n        fields: ['taskNumber', 'name']\n      },\n      projectCostOrganization: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      projectCostType: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      businessUnit: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      transactionSource: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      document: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      contract: {\n        fields: ['contractName','contractNumber','publicIdentifier']\n      },\n      fundingSource: {\n        fields: ['fundingSourceNumber']\n      },\n      person: {\n        accessors: {\n          names: {\n            fields: ['displayName']\n          },\n          personDetail: {\n            fields: ['personNumber']\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      transactionCurrency: {\n        fields: ['currencyCode']\n      }\n    },\n    collection: {\n      limit: 21\n    }\n  };\n} else if (artifact === 'unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails') {\n  target = {\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectCostTransactions',\n    businessObject: 'UnprocessedProjectCostTransaction',\n    businessView: 'unprocessedProjectCostTransactionDetails'\n  };\n  queryConfig = {\n    fields: [\n      'unprocessedTransactionReferenceId',\n      'batchName',\n      'transactionDate',\n      'quantity',\n      'rawCostInTransactionCurrency'\n    ],\n    accessors: {\n      project: {\n        fields: ['projectNumber', 'name']\n      },\n      task: {\n        fields: ['taskNumber', 'name']\n      },\n      projectCostOrganization: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      projectCostType: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      businessUnit: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      transactionSource: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      document: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      contract: {\n        fields: ['contractName','contractNumber','publicIdentifier']\n      },\n      fundingSource: {\n        fields: ['fundingSourceNumber']\n      },\n      person: {\n        accessors: {\n          names: {\n            fields: ['displayName']\n          },\n          personDetail: {\n            fields: ['personNumber']\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      transactionCurrency: {\n        fields: ['currencyCode']\n      }\n    },\n    collection: {\n      limit: 21\n    }\n  };\n} else if (artifact === 'projectAssetsView') {\n  target = {\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectAsset',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectAsset',\n    businessView: 'projectAssetsView'\n  };\n\n  queryConfig = {\n    fields: [\n      'assetName',\n      'actualInServiceOrRetirementDate',\n      'totalAssetCost',\n      'capitalizedCost',\n      'reversalDate',\n      'capitalHoldFlag',\n      'description',\n      'assetNumber',\n      'actualUnits',\n      'manufacturerName',\n      'modelNumber',\n      'serialNumber',\n      'tagNumber'\n    ],\n    accessors: {\n      project: {\n        fields: ['name','projectNumber'],\n        accessors: {\n           projectLedgerCurrency: {\n             fields: ['currencyCode']\n           }\n        }\n      },\n      businessUnit: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      },\n      assetType: {\n        fields: ['meaning']\n      },\n      assetBook: {\n        fields: ['name']\n      }\n    },\n    collection: {\n      limit: 21\n    }\n  };\n} else if (artifact === 'projectAssetAssignmentsView') {\n  target = {\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectAsset',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectAssetAssignment',\n    businessView: 'projectAssetAssignmentsView'\n  };\n\n  queryConfig = {\n    fields: ['commonCostFlag'],\n    accessors: {\n      project: {\n        fields: ['projectNumber','name']\n      },\n      task: {\n        fields: ['taskNumber','name']\n      },\n      projectAsset: {\n        fields: ['assetName']\n      }\n    },\n    collection: {\n      limit: 21\n    }\n  };\n} else if (artifact === 'projectAssetLinesView') {\n  target = {\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectAsset',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectAssetLine',\n    businessView: 'projectAssetLinesView'\n  };\n\n  queryConfig = {\n    fields: [\n      'id',\n      'description',\n      'amount',\n      'originalAmount',\n      'assetPeriodName'\n    ],\n    accessors: {\n      project: {\n        fields: ['name','projectNumber'],\n        accessors: {\n           projectLedgerCurrency: {\n             fields: ['currencyCode']\n           }\n        }\n      },\n      projectTask: {\n        fields: ['name','taskNumber']\n      },\n      projectAsset: {\n        fields: ['assetName']\n      },\n      status: {\n        fields: ['meaning']\n      },\n      cipCostAccount: {\n        fields: ['concatenatedSegments']\n      }\n    },\n    collection: {\n      limit: 21\n    }\n  };\n} else if (artifact === 'projectContractInvoiceDetails') {\n  target = {\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectBillingTransactions',\n    businessObject: 'ProjectContractInvoice',\n    businessView: 'projectContractInvoiceDetails'\n  };\n\n  queryConfig = {\n    fields: [\n      'invoiceNumber',\n      'invoiceDate',\n      'transferStatus',\n      'accountingPeriod'\n    ],\n    accessors: {\n      project: {\n        fields: ['projectNumber']\n      },\n      contract: {\n        fields: ['contractNumber']\n      },\n      status: {\n        fields: ['meaning']\n      }\n    },\n    collection: {\n      limit: 21\n    }\n  };\n} else if (artifact === 'ProjectCostTransactionSummary') {\n  target = {\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectCostTransactions',\n    analyticView: 'ProjectCostTransactionSummary'\n  };\n} else if (artifact === 'ProjectAssetLineSummary') {\n  target = {\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectAsset',\n    analyticView: 'ProjectAssetLineSummary'\n  };\n} else if (artifact === 'ProjectContractInvoiceSummary') {\n  target = {\n    module: 'oraErpCoreProjectBillingTransactions',\n    analyticView: 'ProjectContractInvoiceSummary'\n  };\n} else {\n  throw new Error('Unsupported artifact returned by PRJ_PJC_LLM_IDENTIFY_ARTIFACT: ' + (artifact || 'empty value'));\n}\n\nconst bossQuery = { target };\nif (queryConfig) {\n  bossQuery.query = queryConfig;\n}\n\nconst payload = {\n  question: userMessage,\n  queries: [bossQuery]\n};\n\nreturn JSON.stringify(payload);"
          },
